# Database Rules

- Use the existing Supabase PostgreSQL configuration.
- Inspect existing migrations and schema before changing the database.
- Never assume a conceptual table already exists.
- Avoid duplicate tables and conflicting migrations.
- Use versioned SQL migrations.
- Apply appropriate foreign keys and indexes.
- Preserve user and provider ownership boundaries.
- Use Row-Level Security where Supabase client access is permitted.
- Do not rely exclusively on frontend authorization.
- Never commit service-role credentials or production secrets.
- Keep demo seed data separate from schema migrations.
